    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="16" spacingafter="2" fontweight="bold">D2 I-95 PEDESTRIAN BRIDGE</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">C013 - Pier Pile Design</paragraph>
    <section name="WorkingNotes" capture="False" hide="true">
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#43505C">Working notes (hidden; not part of the submitted calculation): how this edition was produced, its tool status and the open bookkeeping items.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Distilled from the pile design notebook (package 8db9964e721f), case "Pier piles: 20 in steel pipe, FBMP fixed run". Same inputs, equations and load combinations as the notebook; results should match its exported report. Blockpad edition written by pile_design/bpad.py (scripts/build_pile_bpad.py) from the same case; every definition was evaluated independently and compared with the notebook to 1 part in 10⁹.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Status: All numerical checks pass (largest ratio 1.00) · 16 pending item(s) remain.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• FBMP source: Pier_Fixed.XML, SHA-256 bb73e6ada6cf35ebb80b512cee315075807fc8ccab7878406d81ff381ae40fe7 (registered export PIER-XML). 4 piles at 5 ft; cutoff elevation 41.7717 ft, ground 26.05 ft.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Every definition was read back from the XML and evaluated by an independent Blockpad-syntax evaluator, then compared with the notebook (and with the Mathcad worksheet) before the file was written. Governing records, the notebook angles, the neutral-axis depth c_gov and the few values found by a search over the interaction sweep are amber inputs read from the notebook.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">The notebook lists 16 PENDING items; the distilled ratios above do not close them: Local buckling class · nonslender (D/t vs 0.11 E/Fy); Slenderness KL/r ≤ 120; Axial compression · maximum Pu / φc Pn; Combined axial load and flexure · Eq. 6.9.2.2.1 (-1); Shear · round tube; Tension · maximum strength uplift; Pile Data Table completeness (SDM 11.4); Steel grade and Fy reconciled; Corrosion allowance; Environment classification; Pile-to-cap connection (12 in embedment); Downdrag source documented; FBMP export current; Minimum tip elevation; Scour resistance and elevations; Drivability.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">The Status covers the recomputed numerical checks only; it is not design acceptance.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Inputs pending confirmation (captions carried "[pending confirmation]" in the notebook): DD_tons, R_scour_net_tons, R_scour_total_tons, soil_type, S_u, environment, t_corr, Fy, L_v.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">A ✓ status covers only the recomputed numerical checks; it is not design acceptance. The pending items of the notebook stay open. Recalculate in Blockpad after any input change.</paragraph>
    </section>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Project: D2 I-95 Pedestrian Bridge.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Codes: AASHTO LRFD Bridge Design Specifications, 10th edition (2024): 6.5.4.2, 6.8.2.1, 6.9.2.2.1, 6.9.4.1, 6.12.1.2.3b, 6.12.2.2.3, 10.7.3.13; FDOT Structures Design Guidelines (SDG) 3.5 and Structures Detailing Manual (SDM) 11.4, January 2026; Specification 455-8.2 (Table 962-11).</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Inputs are highlighted amber; results are the green tables.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True">1. Design basis</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• FBMP analysis: Pier_Fixed.XML. 4 piles at 5 ft; cutoff elevation 41.7717 ft, ground 26.05 ft.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Pile: ASTM A252 / API 5L pipe 20 in x 0.48 in wall, Fy = 45 ksi (noncomposite).</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Downdrag 0 tons per pile is a drag load DR: gamma_DR = 1.1 (strength) and 1 (Service I) in the structural demands (LRFD Table 3.4.1-1, 10.7.3.7); it is excluded from the Factored Design Load and added nominally to the required bearing resistance (SDG Eq. 3-1, phi = 0.75).</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Second-order effects come from the FBMP P-delta analysis; the LRFD column check here uses K(Lu + Lf). Composite (filled) pipe is out of scope.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True">2. Inputs</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="3" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">Pile and layout</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
      <dynexp formula="D_pile = 20 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
        <expbody>D_pile = 20 in</expbody>
      </dynexp>
    </paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Pile size (square side, or pipe outside diameter)</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="N_pile = 4" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>N_pile = 4</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Piles in the support</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="S_pile = 5 ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>S_pile = 5 ft</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Center-to-center pile spacing</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="EL_cutoff = 41.771667 ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>EL_cutoff = 41.771667 ft</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Pile cutoff elevation (FBMP pile head)</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="EL_ground = 26.05 ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>EL_ground = 26.05 ft</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Ground elevation (top of soil layer 1)</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
      <dynexp formula="L_unsupported = 15.721667 ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
        <expbody>L_unsupported = 15.721667 ft</expbody>
      </dynexp>
    </paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Length above ground (cutoff - ground); editable</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="embed_cap = 12 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>embed_cap = 12 in</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Pile embedment into the cap</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="3" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">Loads and geotechnical</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="DD_tons = 0" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>DD_tons = 0</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Downdrag (drag load DR) per pile, short tons</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
      <dynexp formula="gamma_DR_str = 1.1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
        <expbody>gamma_DR_str = 1.1</expbody>
      </dynexp>
    </paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Drag-load factor, strength limit states (structural)</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="gamma_DR_ser = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>gamma_DR_ser = 1</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Drag-load factor, Service I</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
      <dynexp formula="phi_geo = 0.75" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
        <expbody>phi_geo = 0.75</expbody>
      </dynexp>
    </paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Geotechnical resistance factor (compression, Davisson)</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="R_scour_net_tons = 0" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>R_scour_net_tons = 0</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Net scour resistance, short tons</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="R_scour_total_tons = 0" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>R_scour_total_tons = 0</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Total scour resistance, short tons</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="K_eff = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>K_eff = 1</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Effective length factor K</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="soil_type = 0" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>soil_type = 0</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Soil for depth to fixity (0 sand, 1 clay)</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="n_h = 0.556 ksi/ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>n_h = 0.556 ksi/ft</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Rate of increase of soil modulus, sand</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
      <dynexp formula="S_u = 1 kip/ft^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
        <expbody>S_u = 1 kip/ft^2</expbody>
      </dynexp>
    </paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Undrained shear strength, clay (used only for soil type 1)</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="3" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">Environment and policy</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="environment = 2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>environment = 2</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Environment classification</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="3" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">Steel pipe pile</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="D_out = 20 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>D_out = 20 in</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Pipe outside diameter</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="t_wall = 0.48 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>t_wall = 0.48 in</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Pipe wall thickness (nominal)</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="t_corr = 0 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>t_corr = 0 in</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Corrosion allowance deducted from the wall</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="Fy = 45 ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>Fy = 45 ksi</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Steel yield strength</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="E_s = 29000 ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>E_s = 29000 ksi</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Steel modulus</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
      <dynexp formula="phi_c_axial = 0.7" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
        <expbody>phi_c_axial = 0.7</expbody>
      </dynexp>
    </paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Axial compression resistance factor, pipe (good driving, no tip)</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
      <dynexp formula="phi_c_comb = 0.8" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
        <expbody>phi_c_comb = 0.8</expbody>
      </dynexp>
    </paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Axial resistance factor, combined axial and flexure</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="φ_f = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>φ_f = 1</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Flexure resistance factor</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="phi_v_steel = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>phi_v_steel = 1</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Shear resistance factor, steel</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="phi_y = 0.95" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>phi_y = 0.95</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Tension yielding resistance factor</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
      <dynexp formula="L_v = 15.721667 ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
        <expbody>L_v = 15.721667 ft</expbody>
      </dynexp>
    </paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Shear span Lv (distance from maximum to zero shear)</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True">3. Demands from the FBMP export</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Governing records of Pier_Fixed.XML for each check (records 1 to 4). FBMP axial force is converted to compression positive. The drag load DR = DD is added to the axial force at every station (LRFD Table 3.4.1-1, 10.7.3.7): gamma_DR for the limit state of the record. Downdrag is not in the Factored Design Load.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Axial: combo 2 STRENGTH-III · pile 4 · element 13J · EL 16.55 ft.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Combined: combo 2 STRENGTH-III · pile 4 · element 13J · EL 16.55 ft.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Shear: combo 2 STRENGTH-III · pile 4 · element 1I · EL 41.77 ft (+1 tied).</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Tension: combo 3 STRENGTH-III · pile 1 · element 12I · EL 22.88 ft.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="3" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">Governing FBMP records, one row per check (inputs read from the export)</paragraph>
    <embed spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="8">
      <table name="DemandInputs" capture="False" colwidths="1:120, 2:88, 3:88, 4:88, 5:88, 6:88">
        <stylerule range="A1:F5" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#A78638&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.4, &quot;#A78638&quot;);"/>
        <stylerule range="A1:F1" horzalign="Center" vertalign="Center"/>
        <stylerule range="B2:F5" horzalign="Center" vertalign="Center"/>
        <row>
          <textcell name="DemandInputsR0C0" capture="False" background="#F7E6B9">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold" horzalign="Center">Record</paragraph>
          </textcell>
          <textcell name="DemandInputsR0C1" capture="False" background="#F7E6B9">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold" horzalign="Center">P_fbmp (kip)</paragraph>
          </textcell>
          <textcell name="DemandInputsR0C2" capture="False" background="#F7E6B9">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold" horzalign="Center">M_2 (kip*ft)</paragraph>
          </textcell>
          <textcell name="DemandInputsR0C3" capture="False" background="#F7E6B9">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold" horzalign="Center">M_3 (kip*ft)</paragraph>
          </textcell>
          <textcell name="DemandInputsR0C4" capture="False" background="#F7E6B9">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold" horzalign="Center">M_res (kip*ft)</paragraph>
          </textcell>
          <textcell name="DemandInputsR0C5" capture="False" background="#F7E6B9">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold" horzalign="Center">V_res (kip)</paragraph>
          </textcell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <textcell name="DemandInputsR1C0" capture="False" background="#FFF8E9">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0">1. Axial</paragraph>
          </textcell>
          <textcell name="DemandInputsR1C1" capture="False" background="#FFF8E9">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="2">
              <dynexp formula="P_fbmp_1 = 265.58 kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
                <expbody>P_fbmp_1 = 265.58 kip</expbody>
              </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
          </textcell>
          <textcell name="DemandInputsR1C2" capture="False" background="#FFF8E9">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="2">
